","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timur","c":2},{"y":1402,"t":"gain","x":"1402: Khwarazm is Timurid on Cliopatria's map.","cp":"Khwarazm (Urgench, Sufi dynasty)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timurid_Empire","c":1},{"y":1402,"t":"gain","x":"1402: the Aral and Syr Darya steppe joins Cliopatria's shape.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timurid_Empire","c":1},{"y":1402,"t":"gain","x":"1402: Cliopatria's shape adds the Punjab and an Indian fringe after Timur's 1398-1399 raid.","cp":"tughlaq-dynasty","cpn":"Tughlaq dynasty","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timur","c":1},{"y":1402,"t":"occupation_start","x":"20 July 1402: Timur defeats Bayezid at Ankara.","m":7,"cp":"ottoman-empire","cpn":"Ottoman Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timur","c":2},{"y":1403,"t":"vassal_start","x":"1403: Georgia becomes tributary.","cp":"kingdom-of-georgia","cpn":"Kingdom of Georgia","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timur's_invasions_of_Georgia","c":3},{"y":1403,"t":"occupation_end","x":"1403: Anatolia is left.","cp":"ottoman-empire","cpn":"Ottoman Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timur","c":1},{"y":1405,"t":"loss","x":"1405: Khalil Sultan seizes Samarkand.","cp":"Khalil Sultan (rival Timurid emperor)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shah_Rukh_(Timurid_dynasty)","c":3},{"y":1405,"t":"capital_move","x":"1405: the capital passes to Herat.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timurid_Empire","c":2},{"y":1405,"t":"loss","x":"1405: George VII recovers Nakhchivan and Ganja.","cp":"kingdom-of-georgia","cpn":"Kingdom of Georgia","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timur's_invasions_of_Georgia","c":2},{"y":1405,"t":"vassal_end","x":"1405: Georgia's tribute lapses.","cp":"kingdom-of-georgia","cpn":"Kingdom of Georgia","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timur's_invasions_of_Georgia","c":2},{"y":1405,"t":"loss","x":"1405: Iraq slips away.","cp":"jalayirid-sultanate","cpn":"Jalayirid Sultanate","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qara_Qoyunlu","c":1},{"y":1406,"t":"loss","x":"14 October 1406: Qara Yusuf retakes Tabriz.","m":10,"cp":"qara-qoyunlu","cpn":"Qara Qoyunlu","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qara_Qoyunlu","c":3},{"y":1407,"t":"loss","x":"1407: the Punjab leaves the Timurid shape.","cp":"tughlaq-dynasty","cpn":"Tughlaq dynasty","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timur","c":1},{"y":1407,"t":"loss","x":"1407-1415: Khuzestan, Gilan and the north Caucasus fringe leave Cliopatria's shape.","cp":"unknown (page silent)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qara_Qoyunlu","c":1},{"y":1409,"t":"gain","x":"1409: Shah Rukh takes Samarkand.","cp":"Khalil Sultan (rival Timurid emperor)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shah_Rukh_(Timurid_dynasty)","c":2},{"y":1420,"t":"contest_start","x":"1420: Shah Rukh attacks the Qara Qoyunlu.","cp":"qara-qoyunlu","cpn":"Qara Qoyunlu","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shah_Rukh_(Timurid_dynasty)","c":2},{"y":1435,"t":"contest_end","x":"1434-1435: the third Azerbaijan expedition succeeds.","cp":"qara-qoyunlu","cpn":"Qara Qoyunlu","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qara_Qoyunlu","c":3},{"y":1435,"t":"vassal_start","x":"1435: Jahan Shah rules the Qara Qoyunlu as Shah Rukh's vassal.","cp":"qara-qoyunlu","cpn":"Qara Qoyunlu","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qara_Qoyunlu","c":3},{"y":1446,"t":"loss","x":"1446: Abu'l-Khayr Khan takes the Syr Darya.","cp":"khanate-of-sibir","cpn":"Khanate of Sibir","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abu%27l-Khayr_Khan","c":3},{"y":1447,"t":"vassal_end","x":"1447: Jahan Shah becomes independent.","cp":"qara-qoyunlu","cpn":"Qara Qoyunlu","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qara_Qoyunlu","c":3},{"y":1447,"t":"loss","x":"1447: the Qara Qoyunlu take western Iran.","cp":"qara-qoyunlu","cpn":"Qara Qoyunlu","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qara_Qoyunlu","c":3},{"y":1447,"t":"capital_move","x":"1447: the seat moves to Samarkand.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timurid_Empire","c":2},{"y":1449,"t":"loss","x":"1449: Abdal-Latif Mirza seizes Samarkand.","cp":"Abdal-Latif Mirza (Timurid rival)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abu_Sa%27id_Mirza","c":2},{"y":1450,"t":"loss","x":"1450: Khwarazm and the Syr Darya steppe leave Cliopatria's shape.","cp":"unknown (page silent)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abu_Sa%27id_Mirza","c":1},{"y":1451,"t":"gain","x":"June 1451: Abu Sa'id takes Samarkand.","m":6,"cp":"Abdullah Mirza (Timurid rival)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abu_Sa%27id_Mirza","c":3},{"y":1453,"t":"loss","x":"1452-1453: Jahan Shah takes central and southern Iran.","cp":"qara-qoyunlu","cpn":"Qara Qoyunlu","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qara_Qoyunlu","c":2},{"y":1458,"t":"loss","x":"Summer 1458: Jahan Shah occupies Herat.","cp":"qara-qoyunlu","cpn":"Qara Qoyunlu","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qara_Qoyunlu","c":3},{"y":1458,"t":"gain","x":"1458: Abu Sa'id re-annexes Khorasan.","cp":"qara-qoyunlu","cpn":"Qara Qoyunlu","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abu_Sa%27id_Mirza","c":3},{"y":1459,"t":"capital_move","x":"1459: Herat is the capital again.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timurid_Empire","c":2},{"y":1459,"t":"gain","x":"1459: Abu Sa'id wins at Sarakhs and extends his rule.","cp":"Ala al-Dawla and Ibrahim Mirza (Timurid princes)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abu_Sa%27id_Mirza","c":2},{"y":1468,"t":"contest_start","x":"February 1468: Abu Sa'id marches on the Aq Qoyunlu.","m":2,"cp":"aq-qoyunlu","cpn":"Aq Qoyunlu","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abu_Sa%27id_Mirza","c":2},{"y":1469,"t":"contest_end","x":"5 February 1469: Abu Sa'id is beaten at Qarabagh and executed.","m":2,"cp":"aq-qoyunlu","cpn":"Aq Qoyunlu","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abu_Sa%27id_Mirza","c":3},{"y":1469,"t":"rename","x":"24 March 1469: Husayn Bayqara takes Herat; the empire divides.","m":3,"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Husayn_Bayqara","c":3},{"y":1501,"t":"loss","x":"1501: the Uzbeks take Transoxiana.","cp":"shaybanids","cpn":"Shaybanids","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muhammad_Shaybani","c":3},{"y":1504,"t":"gain","x":"October 1504: Babur captures Kabul.","m":10,"cp":"Kabul (previous holder not named on the page)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Babur","c":3},{"y":1507,"t":"loss","x":"1507: the Uzbeks take Herat.","cp":"shaybanids","cpn":"Shaybanids","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muhammad_Shaybani","c":3},{"y":1507,"t":"capital_move","x":"1507: the seat is Kabul.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Babur","c":2},{"y":1511,"t":"gain","x":"1511: Babur takes Samarkand a third time.","cp":"shaybanids","cpn":"Shaybanids","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Babur","c":3},{"y":1512,"t":"loss","x":"1512: Samarkand and Bukhara are lost again.","cp":"shaybanids","cpn":"Shaybanids","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Babur","c":3},{"y":1521,"t":"gain","x":"1521: Babur takes Badakhshan.","cp":"Uways Mirza (Badakhshan)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Babur","c":3},{"y":1522,"t":"gain","x":"1522: Babur annexes Kandahar.","cp":"Arghun dynasty","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Babur","c":3},{"y":1525,"t":"gain","x":"1525: Babur is master of the Punjab.","cp":"lodi-dynasty","cpn":"Lodi dynasty","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Babur","c":2},{"y":1526,"t":"gain","x":"21 April 1526: Babur wins at Panipat.","m":4,"cp":"lodi-dynasty","cpn":"Lodi dynasty","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Babur","c":3},{"y":1526,"t":"dissolve","x":"1526: the Timurid line becomes the Mughal Empire.","m":4,"cp":"mughal-empire","cpn":"Mughal Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Babur","c":2}],"wars":[{"name":"Timur's conquest of Persia","from":1383,"to":1393,"outcome":"Timur takes Herat and Khorasan from 1383, removes the Kartids by 1389, takes Isfahan in 1387 and Shiraz in 1393, annexing the Muzaffarids.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timur"},{"name":"Tokhtamysh-Timur war","from":1387,"to":1395,"outcome":"Timur destroys Tokhtamysh on the Kondurcha in 1391 and at the Terek in 1395 and sacks Sarai and Astrakhan, but holds no Golden Horde land.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timur"},{"name":"Timur's invasions of Georgia","from":1386,"to":1403,"outcome":"After campaigns in 1386-87, 1394, 1399, 1400-01 and 1403 George VII accepts tribute; 'Georgia became tributary to the Timurids' but kept its independence.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timur's_invasions_of_Georgia"},{"name":"Timur's invasion of India","from":1398,"to":1399,"outcome":"Timur defeats Mahmud Shah, sacks Delhi in December 1398 and leaves in January 1399 without annexing it.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timurid_Empire"},{"name":"Timur's Syrian and Anatolian campaigns, Battle of Ankara","from":1400,"to":1402,"outcome":"Timur sacks Aleppo and Damascus (1400), destroys Baghdad (1401), defeats Bayezid at Ankara (20 July 1402) and takes Smyrna in December 1402; none of it is held.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timur"},{"name":"Timurid war of succession of 1405","from":1405,"to":1409,"outcome":"Khalil Sultan seizes Samarkand in 1405; Pir Muhammad is assassinated in 1407, Miran Shah killed in 1408; Shah Rukh takes Samarkand in 1409 and takes the throne.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shah_Rukh_(Timurid_dynasty)"},{"name":"Shah Rukh's Azerbaijan campaigns against the Qara Qoyunlu","from":1420,"to":1435,"outcome":"Campaigns of 1420-21, 1429-31 and 1434 end with Jahan Shah installed as a Timurid vassal; Tabriz is held only briefly in 1421.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shah_Rukh_(Timurid_dynasty)"},{"name":"Qara Qoyunlu conquest of Timurid western and central Iran","from":1447,"to":1458,"outcome":"Jahan Shah takes the west after Shah Rukh's death, central and southern Iran in 1452-53 and holds Herat for a few months in 1458.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qara_Qoyunlu"},{"name":"Abu Sa'id Mirza's campaign against the Aq Qoyunlu","from":1468,"to":1469,"outcome":"Abu Sa'id is defeated and captured at Qarabagh and executed on 5 February 1469; no territorial change on the frontier.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abu_Sa%27id_Mirza"},{"name":"Husayn Bayqara's struggle for Herat","from":1469,"to":1470,"outcome":"Husayn takes Herat on 24 March 1469, beats Yadgar Muhammad at Chenaran on 15 September 1469, loses Herat on 7 July 1470 and recovers it six weeks later.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Husayn_Bayqara"},{"name":"Uzbek conquest of Transoxiana and Khorasan","from":1500,"to":1507,"outcome":"Shaybani ousts the Timurids from Samarkand (1500), takes Bukhara (1501) and Herat (1507); he dies at Merv on 2 December 1510.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muhammad_Shaybani"},{"name":"Babur's conquests in Kabul and Hindustan","from":1504,"to":1526,"outcome":"Babur takes Kabul in 1504, Badakhshan in 1521, Kandahar in 1522, the Punjab by 1525 and wins at Panipat on 21 April 1526, founding the Mughal Empire.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Babur"}],"certainty":[{"from":1370,"to":1526,"level":"soft","note":"No treaty or survey frontiers on the pages: steppe, mountain and desert edges throughout."}],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timurid_Empire","title":"Timurid Empire"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timur","title":"Timur"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shah_Rukh_(Timurid_dynasty)","title":"Shah Rukh"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abu_Sa%27id_Mirza","title":"Abu Sa'id Mirza"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Husayn_Bayqara","title":"Husayn Bayqara"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muhammad_Shaybani","title":"Muhammad Shaybani"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Babur","title":"Babur"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qara_Qoyunlu","title":"Qara Qoyunlu"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abu%27l-Khayr_Khan","title":"Abu'l-Khayr Khan"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timur's_invasions_of_Georgia","title":"Timur's invasions of Georgia"}]}